1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,890
Do you have any tattoos?
你有纹身吗？

2
00:00:02,890 --> 00:00:04,340
I don't.
我没有。

3
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:07,870
I've never been brave enough to go under the needle.
我从来没有足够的勇气去纹身。

4
00:00:07,870 --> 00:00:11,950
But if you do have one, you are not alone.
但如果你有，你并不孤单。

5
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:24,930
According to a report by Experian, the number of tattoo parlours in Britain increased by 173% between 2004 and 2014.
益博睿（Experian）的一份报告显示，2004年至2014年间，英国的纹身店数量增长了173%。

6
00:00:24,930 --> 00:00:31,170
Tattoos have always been controversial – personally and culturally.
纹身一直颇具争议——无论是在个人层面还是文化层面。

7
00:00:31,170 --> 00:00:34,370
Some people love them and some hate them.
有人喜欢，也有人厌恶。

8
00:00:34,370 --> 00:00:38,360
So, are they good or bad?
那么，纹身究竟是好是坏？

9
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:49,010
These days, one in five people in the UK has some ink – whether it's a commemorative date, a sleeve or a full body suit.
如今，英国五分之一的人都有纹身——无论是纪念日期、半袖纹身还是全身纹身。

10
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:52,980
What's responsible for this rise in popularity?
是什么让纹身如此流行？

11
00:00:52,980 --> 00:01:02,530
"You see a lot of celebrities getting tattooed," says Lee Clements of the British Tattoo Artist Association speaking on BBC radio.
英国纹身艺术家协会的李·克莱门茨在BBC广播中表示：“你会看到很多名人纹身。”

12
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:10,420
As a result, people want to copy them or it becomes a fashion thing – certain tattoos become a trend.
因此，人们想要模仿他们，或者纹身成为一种时尚——某些纹身图案会成为潮流。

13
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:15,430
Employers have become more accepting of visible tats too.
雇主们对可见的纹身也变得更加宽容。

14
00:01:15,430 --> 00:01:22,620
Last year, London's Metropolitan Police relaxed a ban on recruiting candidates with visible body art.
去年，伦敦警察局放宽了对招聘有可见纹身候选人的禁令。

15
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:32,970
And earlier this year, Air New Zealand said it would end a ban on body art to allow workers to express their individuality and cultural heritage.
今年早些时候，新西兰航空表示将取消对纹身的禁令，允许员工表达自己的个性和文化传承。

16
00:01:32,970 --> 00:01:37,190
That said, not all employers would agree.
尽管如此，并非所有雇主都认同这一点。

17
00:01:37,190 --> 00:01:46,970
Grace, 28, told the BBC that she had been offered jobs in sales, which were then withdrawn when employers saw her hand tattoo.
28岁的格雷丝告诉BBC，她曾获得过销售岗位的工作机会，但当雇主看到她手上的纹身后，offer被撤回了。

18
00:01:46,970 --> 00:01:52,700
"It feels like having a tattoo is not socially acceptable," she says.
“感觉纹身在社会上是不被接受的，”她说。

19
00:01:52,700 --> 00:02:03,440
"Having a tattoo does not amount to a protected characteristic," remarks Susan Harris, legal director at the GMB union, a UK trade union.
英国工会GMB的法律总监苏珊·哈里斯表示：“纹身并不是受保护的特征。”

20
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:12,640
This means a person can be dismissed for having one if it breaches the employer's dress code – except on religious grounds.
这意味着，除非出于宗教原因，否则如果纹身违反了雇主的着装规范，员工可能会因此被解雇。

21
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:16,690
And let's not forget the risk of infection.
此外，我们不要忘记感染的风险。

22
00:02:16,690 --> 00:02:26,590
At present anyone in the UK can set up a parlour and offer procedures without proper training, a report from the Royal Society for Public Health says.
英国公共卫生学会的一份报告称，目前在英国，任何人都可以开设纹身店并提供纹身服务，无需接受适当的培训。

23
00:02:26,590 --> 00:02:37,860
They note that just under 20% of those tattooed experience negative side effects, including swelling, burning or a skin infection.
报告指出，近20%的纹身者会经历副作用，包括肿胀、灼痛或皮肤感染。

24
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:44,670
It seems that attitudes to tattoos are changing, but they aren't quite there yet.
人们对纹身的态度似乎正在改变，但还没有完全转变。

25
00:02:44,670 --> 00:02:50,510
Should you be persuaded to have one – visit a reputable tattoo artist with a portfolio.
如果你被说动想要纹身——一定要去找有作品集、信誉良好的纹身师。

26
00:02:50,510 --> 00:02:55,090
Discuss your design with them and don't make a hasty decision!
和他们讨论你的设计，不要仓促做决定！

27
00:02:55,090 --> 00:03:00,120
If you later regret it, your tattoo will need laser removal or a cover up.
如果之后后悔了，你需要通过激光去除纹身或者覆盖纹身。

28
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:06,330
Better get a temporary tattoo or henna tattoo first and see if you're happy with it.
最好先纹一个临时纹身或彩绘，看看自己是否满意。

29
00:03:06,330 --> 00:03:09,780
Wear it for a few months and then decide.
几个月后再做决定。
